// | build --backend llvm std/qa/probe_cap_fs.oo | **FAIL** `ERR build emit-llvm failed` — prints IR then errors; no object-link step on this path |
// | build /tmp/t.oo (outside workspace) | `ERR build unreadable file` — capability-bounded read refuses out-of-scope path (fail-closed, correct) |

// The LLVM repair WIP is internally consistent: every modified file
// still typechecks. The failure is confined to the llvm BUILD path
// (emit works, link/object step does not) — matches the 2026-09-10
// known-broken note; still open on today's installed binary.

// ## 5. Findings by severity

// MAJOR (0): none new. The emit-llvm build failure is a carried
//   known-issue with an owner (compiler lane, mcp AGENT.md 2026-09-10).

// MINOR (3):
//   m1. qa/scratch_lineno.oo — committed scratch file, no Academy
//       header, name says "scratch" (§1.11, P10). Either delete or
//       promote to a real probe with header + suite wiring.
//   m2. File: drift ×3 (TOKEN_OPT.oot, CAP_LEGACY_SUPERSEDE_REMOVAL_
//       TODO.oot, bootstrap/seed/{README,SIGNING}.oot) — §1.4.
//   m3. bootstrap/corpus/ has no ANCHOR.oo — 104 headerless fixtures
//       are defensible, but nothing on disk documents the fixture
//       exemption; a header checker's only signal is path shape.

// NOTE (2):
//   n1. `oodac build` fails closed on out-of-workspace paths
//       ("unreadable file") — capability-bounded fs reads working as
//       specified; message could name the cap denial for debuggability.
//   n2. `oodac version` → `ERR cmd residual: version` — no version
//       subcommand while ooda(1) has one; asymmetric UX, and §1.21
//       wants versions derived — consider `oodac version` reading the
//       tag/env like ooda does.

// ## 6. Recommended repairs (oodac lane)

// 1. Delete qa/scratch_lineno.oo (its lineno-scratch purpose is
//    served by corpus) or header it and wire into qa/suite.oo (m1).
// 2. Fix the 3 File: lines to their real repo paths (m2).
// 3. Add bootstrap/corpus/ANCHOR.oo stating the fixture-header
//    exemption explicitly (m3).
// 4. Land the LLVM repair: `build --backend llvm` must reach an
//    object step or fail with a named stage (the current
//    "emit-llvm failed" after printing full IR conflates emit and
//    link failures).

// ## 7. New finding (cross-repo, found during std fix pass)

//   C-NEW (CRITICAL): functions defined in files named ANCHOR.oo
//   typecheck but never reach the C emitter. `oodac check` resolves
//   them; `oodac build` emits bare unprefixed call sites with no
//   definition (gcc: implicit declaration). Controlled repro in
//   std/scratch: identical wrapper fn in hub/ANCHOR.oo fails emit
//   while hub/hub.oo emits fine — the basename is the trigger, not
//   re-export structure. Impact: every X_mod_* wrapper convention
//   across std (net_mod_*, agent_mod_*, test_mod_*, sec_mod_*…) is
//   unbuildable for consumers; probe_repl_m1_audit is blocked by it.
//   The emitter likely special-cases ANCHOR.oo as index-only and
//   skips its function bodies. Fix in the emit pass, not in std.
